runtime: discover children across all process tasks

The leader task child list misses processes spawned by a retained worker.
Read every task at each recursive level and keep the captured process
identities across exit and reparenting.

Observed task disappearance or task-set changes cannot authorize completion.
Require a fresh quiesced proof before machine cleanup and retain the proof
afterward, using the existing tracker and once-only finalization path.
State schemas and cleanup authority remain unchanged.
